;; The GHC 9.14.1 installation the native reads read (HFS-I2 (a), doc/haskell/NATIVE.md, "The native reads' inputs: derived"):
;; the facts arbace.repr.haskell.target derives its tree from, beside the pinned source tarball (the corpus's) and musl 1.2.6's
;; (C's). Each fact is a name or a choice of the installation, not a product read in place: the reads quote the unit ids and the
;; ABI directory in their :cpp records (the -I directories), the target triples in ghcplatform.h, the toolchain's commands in the
;; settings file (the driver reads "Haskell CPP command"/"flags", the target's triple, OS and arch, "base unit-id"). Their origin is
;; Alpine's ghc 9.14.1 package (x86_64), its registered units and its bindist configuration, as the corpus's configuration
;; (test/haskell/corpus-ghc-9.14.1.edn's -I paths) already names them. The :abi hashes are GHC's fingerprints of the units'
;; interfaces: printed in each unit's record for the oracle tier's byte comparison, read by nothing (arbace.repr.haskell.driver's
;; installation reads id, name, version, exposed, include-dirs and depends). A unit without modules has the fingerprint of nothing,
;; 58d8da4e4c1c51b92726bb8097eb8f26 (rts, ghc-prim, ghc-bignum), computed, not listed. Read with the Clojure reader.
{:ghc "9.14.1"
 :libdir "/usr/lib/ghc-9.14.1/lib"
 ;; hadrian's per-installation library directory (Hadrian.Haskell.Hash's ABI directory)
 :abi-dir "x86_64-linux-ghc-9.14.1-07a2"
 ;; the docs directory relative to the package database's pkgroot (bindist Makefile's patchpackageconf $4)
 :docs-rel "../../../share/doc/ghc-9.14.1"
 ;; configure's canonical build and host (ghcplatform.h, the settings' target platform string)
 :build "x86_64-unknown-linux"
 :host "x86_64-alpine-linux"
